From: linux-gaokun-buildbot <186526@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: mark fbdev screen buffer as virtual

msm_fbdev provides a kernel virtual mapping through screen_buffer, but does
not set FBINFO_VIRTFB. The fbdev core consequently selects the I/O helpers
and reports that the framebuffer is not in virtual address space when the
console draws. Mark the mapping explicitly so the system-memory helpers are
used.

Signed-off-by: linux-gaokun-buildbot <186526@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
index 000000000000..111111111111 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
@@ -134,6 +134,7 @@ int msm_fbdev_driver_fbdev_probe(struct drm_fb_helper *helper,
 	fbi->fbops = &msm_fb_ops;
 
 	drm_fb_helper_fill_info(fbi, helper, sizes);
+	fbi->flags |= FBINFO_VIRTFB;
 
 	fbi->screen_buffer = msm_gem_get_vaddr(bo);
 	if (IS_ERR(fbi->screen_buffer)) {
--
2.47.3
